# No live host filesystem access

## Forbidden (never do this)

Do **not** read, list, search, `stat`, `cat`, `grep`, or otherwise inspect:

- `/etc/nixos/**` (and any symlink into it)
- `/run/current-system/**`
- `/nix/var/nix/profiles/system*`
- Other hosts' live config under `/etc/`, `/var/lib/nixos*`, `/run/ncc/**` unless the user **explicitly** pastes paths/output into chat
- Other users' `/proc/<pid>/environ` or running NCC GUI process state on the machine

`ncc system-update` (local/remote) is the user's deploy path. After they update from the repo, treat the **git workspace** as source of truth — not the live machine.

## Required instead

- Work only in the **repository** (`NixOSControlCenter/`, especially `nixos/`).
- If live-host facts are needed (generation, catalog in use, GUI state, `/etc/nixos` contents): **ask the user** to paste output. Do not discover it yourself.
- Validate with repo-only tools: `nix-instantiate` / tests / builds against files **in the workspace**.

## Why

Live `/etc/nixos` is private host state (fleet machines). Agents must not poke the running system to "verify" deploys.
